git commit -m "Static-on-Netlify migration, Phase 2 (cleanup). DNS swap completed earlier today: tools.longboardtechnology.com now resolves to Netlify (custom domain on the new Tools project, Let's Encrypt cert provisioned). Strip the static-serving routes from site_app.py (/, /shared.css, /shared.js, /assets/<path>, /pivot-cup/, /riser-pad/) so Render's role is now /api/* only -- matching the Netlify _redirects proxy that keeps page-side fetches same-origin. The static routes survive in a __main__-gated block at the bottom of site_app.py, repointed at ../Tools/ instead of the old ./site/, so `python site_app.py` (Run Flask.bat) still serves the full site at localhost:5000 for local backend iteration; gunicorn never enters __main__ in production, so those routes don't ship. deploy/Render/site/ deleted in full -- Tools/ (Netlify build context) is now the single source of truth for static surfaces. render.yaml healthCheckPath repointed / -> /api/health to match the new shape (the old / route no longer exists on the API server). site_app.py docstring rewritten to describe the API-only-in-production reality and the local-dev __main__ block. The /assets/<path> route was dead code (pointed at site/assets/ which never existed) and is dropped entirely."
